{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>On the day of his cleansing.</b> This teaches that his cleansing, his uncleanness, the slaughter of the birds, the sprinkling of the birds' blood, and his shaving are all by day. <b>On the day of his cleansing.</b> This teaches that he must not delay." "<b>And he shall be brought to the priest.</b> — the items of his cleansing are brought to the priest, but the person with tzara'at himself is forbidden to enter the camp. And so it is written immediately after: ״ויצא הכהן אל מחוץ למחנה.״ Another interpretation: <b>and he shall be brought to the priest</b> — since his dwelling is outside the camp, on the day of his cleansing they bring him to the edge of the camp and the priest goes out to meet him."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:12:06.747793993Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}